window.TC_PORTRAITS=Object.assign(window.TC_PORTRAITS||{},{"gemini-aries-aries":["You are already halfway through the door, asking a question over your shoulder, and the answer will have to catch up. The Aries Rising leads with the body: quick, direct, forward-leaning, ready before anyone has finished introducing you. The Aries Moon needs the same thing from the inside, momentum and honesty and room to react, so the feeling and the face match. Your Gemini Sun supplies the talk, the jokes and a dozen reasons to try the next thing. People meet readiness. Only later do they notice how fast you are learning.","Two of your lights sit in Aries, so the feeling and the manner move together, with no gap between what you need and how you arrive, and no outside view of how fast that looks. The Gemini Sun makes a friendly sextile to both, so curiosity helps the fire along rather than arguing with it. Mars rules the pair. What this chart lacks is a pause: it can have an opinion, a plan and a first step before a second thought has been invited.","Quick courage with a mind behind it. You start conversations, projects and arguments with equal ease, you learn on the move, and you are rarely embarrassed by being a beginner. People find you refreshing, and often follow you to places they would never have planned.","Speed becomes the habit and the habit becomes a style, so every feeling is acted on and every question answered before it is understood. Impatience can read as dismissal. Growth is a deliberate beat before replying, in which you ask what the other person actually said."],"gemini-aries-taurus":["People hear the low, unhurried voice and assume the mind behind it is just as unhurried. They have not seen the Gemini Sun running three trains of thought at once, or the Aries Moon with a hand already on the emergency cord. The Taurus Rising is real: it slows the room, softens the delivery and makes you look as if you have all afternoon. Inside, you are impatient to ask, try and move. The voice and the impatience tend to arrive together, and people forgive the second because of the first.","Aries, Taurus and Gemini are three neighbouring signs, so each light sees only the one beside it: the Aries Moon barely meets the Gemini Sun, and the Taurus Rising stands between them like a well-mannered doorman. Sun and Moon are a friendly sextile, so thought and feeling cooperate quickly. The Rising slows the delivery rather than the speed. Venus rules the manner and Mars the need, which gives you gentleness at the door and a flare in the kitchen.","A calm front with a fast engine. You can say a bold thing in a way that is easy to hear, start something with energy and let the manner keep the peace. You are persuasive, warm and good at making an urgent idea feel safe to adopt.","The pleasant voice can hide impatience until it has become irritation, and the Moon’s anger arrives as a tight smile. Growth is letting the speed show a little, early, so that people learn the real tempo, and saying the plain sentence in the same lovely voice."],"gemini-taurus-aries":["You are the quickest voice in the room and the one who cannot be hurried to lunch. The Aries Rising arrives at speed, direct and ready, with a Gemini Sun that has three questions and a joke prepared. Then the Taurus Moon asserts itself: it needs a proper meal, a chair that fits and a body at ease, and it will wait for these with the calm of an old tree. People assume you are all motion. You are a fast mind in a slow-feeling body, and you eat as though the afternoon depended on it.","Aries, Taurus and Gemini are three neighbouring signs, so each light sees only the one beside it: the Rising barely notices that the Moon is a sign away, and the Moon barely hears the Sun. The Sun and Rising are a friendly sextile, so quick things line up easily. The Taurus Moon, exalted and comfortable, is the light that wants nothing to change. Mars hurries the manner, Venus slows the need, and Mercury interprets between them, usually with a joke.","Speed with staying power. You can think on your feet and then sit down and finish the job. You are sociable, sensual and strikingly practical for someone so curious, and you give people the sense of being entertained and looked after in the same evening.","The face runs ahead, the Moon digs its heels in behind it, and the Sun explains both with a good story. You may agree to the new plan with your whole manner while your body quietly refuses it. Growth is checking with the Moon first, asking whether this is comfortable, and letting the answer set the pace."],"gemini-taurus-taurus":["You carry it in the shoulders and the throat: shoulders that drop when the room is comfortable, and a throat that opens when the conversation is good. Moon and Rising both sit in Taurus, so the feeling and the face are calm, sensual and unhurried, fond of good food, soft fabric and routine. Your Gemini Sun is the bird in the courtyard of this settled house, asking questions, trading news and chasing every new thing that flies over. The house stays still. The bird goes out and comes back with something to say.","Moon and Rising share Taurus, so the need and the manner are one calm voice, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as unhurried as you seem. The Gemini Sun is a neighbour to both, so it barely sees what its own house is doing, and the chart holds a curious mind surrounded by two lights that want things to stay. Venus rules the pair and the Moon is exalted, which gives comfort a deep authority. Mercury has to argue its case with charm.","Soothing intelligence. You can explain anything in a way that feels like a hand on the shoulder, you are good with money, food, voices and the pace of a room, and you bring ideas into the world without upsetting it. People relax near you and then discover how much they have learned.","Two comfortable lights can outvote the curious one, so questions get postponed in favour of the routine. The Sun then talks about change at length without altering the furniture. Growth is one real experiment a month, something that makes the body slightly uncomfortable, and staying with it long enough to learn from it."],"gemini-gemini-aries":["People assume you talk too much to be serious. Talking is simply how you think. Sun and Moon both sit in Gemini, so the self and the need share one curious voice that learns by saying things aloud, trying them on and trading them for better ones. The Aries Rising gives that voice a running start: you arrive mid-sentence, with a question already in your hand. The result is quick, funny and sometimes more honest than intended. The seriousness shows up in the follow-through.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, so mind and feeling use the same channel: what you feel arrives as a sentence, and what you think arrives as a mood. There is no gap and no outside view, so the chart rarely hears a dissenting voice. The Aries Rising is a friendly sextile to both and gives the pair a body: speed, a direct manner, a readiness to act on the idea in the same minute. Mercury rules the doubled light and Mars the entrance, so the words come armed.","Verbal courage. You say the thing nobody else will, you ask the naive question that cracks the problem open and you learn from every answer. You are an excellent starter of conversations, movements and friendships, and your enthusiasm is usually contagious.","A doubled Gemini can talk its way past a feeling, and the Rising helps it get away faster. You may announce a decision to avoid having a mood about it. Growth is staying silent for one full minute after something hurts, and noticing what the feeling says before you do."],"gemini-gemini-taurus":["At ten past eleven at night you are still on the phone, in a conversation that began at nine, with the tea gone cold and your voice low and easy. Sun and Moon both sit in Gemini, so thinking and feeling share one restless, curious channel. The Taurus Rising is what keeps it from sounding restless: a calm, warm, unhurried manner, a lovely voice, and a body that settles into a chair as if it had nowhere else to be. People think you are relaxed. You are fascinated, and it is a different thing.","Sun and Moon share Gemini, so mind and feeling use one channel and one speed, with no outside view. The Taurus Rising stands a sign away from both, so the unhurried, sensual face rarely matches the quick, curious pair behind it, and each barely sees the other. Mercury rules the doubled light and Venus the manner, which is why the words come out sounding like music. The effect is a very fast mind in a slow, pleasant body.","The gift of the easy ear. You listen as though there were all the time in the world, then answer with something that surprises the speaker. You are fluent, funny and kind, and you can calm a heated conversation just by staying in it with that unhurried voice.","A doubled Gemini will talk about a feeling in place of having one, and the Rising lends the performance a convincing calm. Nobody, including you, can tell when you are overwhelmed. Growth is noticing the body’s signals, the clenched jaw and the skipped meal, before the mind has found words for them."],"gemini-cancer-aries":["You carry it in two places: a tight, tender spot low in the stomach, and a front foot that is already moving, as if the feeling could be outrun. The Cancer Moon keeps everything: old photographs, tones of voice, the exact words said at a funeral. The Aries Rising squares it and sprints past the whole drawer, bright, direct and apparently carefree. Your Gemini Sun narrates the chase with great charm. People get the sprint. A few are shown the album.","The Cancer Moon and Aries Rising square each other, both cardinal, so what you need and how you arrive pull at right angles: the Moon wants to stay close and be held, the Rising wants to be somewhere else, first. The Gemini Sun neighbours the Moon and makes a friendly sextile to the Rising, so it is the translator, quick with words for either side and sometimes too quick to name a feeling before it has been felt. The Moon is at home in its own sign and quietly stronger than it looks.","Tenderness with momentum. You remember what matters to people and then do something about it quickly. You can make a family out of friends, tell the story of a home so vividly that strangers miss it, and be brave on behalf of anyone you have decided to protect.","Feelings are narrated rather than lived, and the Rising leaves the scene before the Moon has finished. You may be brisk with the people you most want to hold. Growth is staying in the room for the second minute, after the joke, and letting a feeling be as slow as it needs to be."],"gemini-cancer-taurus":["A library at dusk: the reading lamps coming on one by one, and outside the window the soil darkening as it rains. The Gemini Sun is the reader moving between the shelves, curious about everything and quick to say what it finds. The Cancer Moon is the drawer of old photographs in the back room, tender, protective and long-remembering. The Taurus Rising is the whole building: warm, unhurried, with a lovely voice and a chair that is always free. People settle in. Only later do they find out how much you have been keeping.","These are three neighbouring signs, Gemini, Cancer and Taurus in a row, so each light sees only the one beside it: the Rising barely meets the Sun, and the Sun barely meets the Moon’s depth. Moon and Rising are a friendly sextile, so feeling and manner cooperate, soft and homely. The Sun is the visitor in this house. Mercury asks questions, the Moon answers in feelings, Venus makes the tea, and the three seldom compare notes.","Warm intelligence. You make learning feel like being looked after, you remember the details of people’s lives and you present them back with great kindness. You are a natural teacher, host and listener, and a safe person to be curious beside.","The Moon stores and the Rising soothes, so a hurt may be tidied away behind hospitality and a clever remark. The Sun finds the story in it later. Growth is letting one real feeling interrupt the conversation, and trusting that the room will stay warm."],"gemini-leo-aries":["The first minute at a party, when the door opens and heads turn, is your favourite minute, and you have long practised looking as though it is an accident. The Aries Rising makes the entrance direct and unhurried by doubt. The Leo Moon, in easy trine with it, needs the warmth and the applause and is wounded by being overlooked. Your Gemini Sun is already in the middle of the room, collecting stories to tell about everyone. You are good company, and a little more sensitive to the audience than you let on.","Fire holds two of your lights: Leo Moon and Aries Rising are a trine, so need and manner flow together with warmth, daring and very little self-doubt. The Gemini Sun makes a sextile to both, an easy angle, so curiosity and humour feed the blaze rather than arguing with it. It is an arc of ease, and its only weakness is that nothing in it slows down. You can be brilliant for an evening and unsure by Tuesday what you actually said.","Warmth that moves. You can charm a room, tell the story that makes it laugh and make each person feel briefly like the guest of honour. You are generous, playful and brave, and you give courage to shy people by making the first move for them.","The Moon needs to be seen and the Rising performs the seeing for it, so applause may be mistaken for contact. The Sun then gathers new material about the audience instead of about yourself. Growth is one conversation a week with no audience, in which you say what you actually need."],"gemini-leo-taurus":["When you are tired you go quiet and generous, when you are delighted you go theatrical, and when you are overlooked you become extremely polite. The Taurus Rising gives you a calm, solid, lovely-voiced front that makes people want to sit down near you. The Leo Moon, squared to it, needs warmth, play and appreciation, and is wounded most by being overlooked. Your Gemini Sun, a friendly sextile from the Moon, writes the notes in the margin: jokes, observations, a compliment saved for later. You are better at being seen than you let on.","Leo Moon and Taurus Rising square each other, both fixed, so the need for applause and the manner of calm are stubborn companions: the Moon wants to shine, the Rising prefers to be dependable and let the work speak. The Gemini Sun makes a sextile with the Moon, so wit and warmth help each other out, and it only half hears the cautious voice of the Rising next door. The effect is a generous, funny person with a good deal of dignity to protect.","Warm, intelligent presence. You make people feel looked at, remembered and funny. You are generous with praise because you know what it is to wait for it, and the calm of the manner lets your warmth arrive without pressure. You can lead a group, a table or a classroom without raising your voice.","The Moon wants to be asked and the Rising will not beg, so you may wait for appreciation until it hardens into a polite chill. The Sun narrates the injury as an anecdote. Growth is asking for what you want, once, in your own lovely voice, and letting someone say yes."],"gemini-virgo-aries":["A shelf of apothecary jars, each labelled in a small, exact hand, and on the draining board beside them a paper boat launched on the washing-up water. That is your household. The Virgo Moon labels, sorts and worries usefully. Your Gemini Sun, ruled by the same Mercury, folds the boat, because ideas want to be tried and not only filed. The Aries Rising is the hand that knocks the jars over in its hurry to see whether the boat floats. People meet speed and bluntness. The care shows later.","Mercury rules both Sun and Moon, so thought and feeling speak a precise, quick language, yet the two signs square each other, both mutable: the Sun wants to explore, the Moon wants to get it right, and each thinks the other is dithering. The Aries Rising is a friendly sextile to the Sun and an awkward fit with the Moon, so the manner you show is bolder than the worry you hold. You are fast in public and a perfectionist in private.","Quick, careful intelligence. You can improvise and then tidy, which is why the work you hand over is both original and correct. You teach, edit, fix and explain with a directness that spares people their own confusion, and you do it with real kindness.","The Moon audits and the Rising pushes on, so criticism is turned inward at night and outward, briskly, by day. Worry is dressed as efficiency. Growth is letting a rough draft stay rough for one afternoon, and telling someone the worry before it has become a list."],"gemini-virgo-taurus":["Is that exactly true, and is it kind, and can I still say it well? You ask it before most sentences, which is why your sentences are so good. The Virgo Moon needs order, usefulness and accuracy, and worries as other people breathe. The Taurus Rising, in easy trine with it, adds calm, a lovely voice and a feeling of reliability. Your Gemini Sun, ruled by the same Mercury as the Moon, wants to say everything and say it now. The compromise is a careful speaker with a quick mind and a needle always threaded.","Mercury rules both Sun and Moon, so thought and feeling share a precise, quick language, yet the two signs square each other, both mutable: the Sun wants to explore, the Moon wants to get it right. The Taurus Rising is a trine to the Moon, so the manner supports the careful side of you with ease, while it stands a single sign from the Sun. It is a grounded arrangement, calm outside, anxious inside, and very good at repairing things.","Careful brilliance. You edit, repair and explain with accuracy and grace, you notice the flaw others miss and you tell them about it in a voice that makes it feel like help. People trust your judgement, and rightly, because you do not say what you have not checked.","The Moon audits and the Rising keeps a composed face, so worry is rarely visible and rarely shared. The Sun then talks about everything except it. Growth is saying “I am worried” in the same calm voice you use for good news, and letting someone else hold the thread."],"gemini-libra-aries":["When you are bored you start a debate, and when you are tired you make peace. The Aries Rising opens the conversation like a door kicked ajar: direct, quick, a little provocative. The Libra Moon, directly opposite, needs the opposite: fairness, a companion and a room with the tension gone. Your Gemini Sun, in easy trine with the Moon, enjoys both and sells each to the other. People see a sparring partner. Those who stay find a diplomat who needs the argument to end well.","Libra Moon and Aries Rising face each other across the wheel, both cardinal, so what you need and how you arrive balance on a narrow beam: harmony against initiative, we against I. The Gemini Sun is a trine to the Moon and a sextile to the Rising, so it has an easy line to both and does the translating, usually with humour. Venus wants the table settled; Mars wants to know who is right. Your skill is to be partisan and fair in the same sentence.","Persuasion with manners. You can disagree vigorously and still leave people feeling respected, argue a case from both sides and then choose one, and break an awkward silence by asking the right question. You make other people braver and more fair-minded at once.","Provocation can become a way of testing closeness, and peace-making a way of avoiding it. The Moon wants calm, the Rising wants a fight, and the Sun keeps talking. Growth is saying what you want before the debate begins, instead of discovering it in the middle."],"gemini-libra-taurus":["Three people share the salon. The Gemini Sun stands at the bookshelf reading aloud to whoever is nearest. The Libra Moon moves the cushions so that nobody is left out and the light is kind to everyone. The Taurus Rising has already put the kettle on and is gazing at the horizon, which is a degree off level and bothers nobody but the Moon. Guests find a courteous, easy, unhurried host. The household knows the Moon is quietly checking that every voice has been heard.","Two air lights and an earth Rising. Gemini Sun and Libra Moon are a trine, so thought and need run together, sociable and fair-minded, while Venus rules both Moon and Rising, which means taste, charm and comfort are all native. The Moon and Rising sit at an awkward remove, though: the Moon wants an open conversation and a balanced room, the Rising wants a stable, familiar one. The adjustments between them are the work of your life.","Gracious sociability. You can host a gathering where nobody is left out, argue both sides with kindness, and make a decision sound like a courtesy. People feel intelligent in your company and at ease, and you remember who sat where and why.","The Moon wants harmony, the Rising wants comfort, and between them the hard conversation can be postponed indefinitely. The Sun supplies a charming reason. Growth is naming a preference before asking the room for theirs, and letting the room be briefly uneasy."],"gemini-scorpio-aries":["How much of this can I say out loud, and who has earned the rest? You ask it constantly, usually mid-sentence. The Gemini Sun and the Aries Rising talk and move at the same easy speed, so you look open, quick and funny. The Scorpio Moon is the courtyard behind the front gate: private, intense, and remembering every word ever said in it. Nobody who hears you talk for an hour suspects how much has been kept back. It is a very particular kind of tact, and it is not deceit.","This is a yod by sign: Gemini Sun and Aries Rising make a friendly sextile, and both stand at an awkward remove from the Scorpio Moon, which sits at the point of the figure. The Moon is therefore the light that cannot be translated into the other two, the one that needs trust, privacy and truth while the others need speed and conversation. Mars rules both Moon and Rising, so the intensity leaks into the manner as heat. The Moon is in its fall, learning through humility.","Charm with depth. You can talk easily to anyone and be trusted by a few completely. You notice what a person avoids saying, you remember the one sentence that mattered, and you can be both the life of the party and the one who sits up with someone at three in the morning.","Easy talk becomes a screen, and the real feeling is kept like a coin in a closed hand. The Rising acts before the Moon has decided, and the Moon files the consequences. Growth is telling one person, early and plainly, what the quiet part of you is holding."],"gemini-scorpio-taurus":["By fifty you will understand that the calm you wore was a vessel, and that the explaining you did was a wire strung to whatever was inside it. The Taurus Rising gives you a low, unhurried voice and a body that settles the room. The Scorpio Moon, directly opposite, feels totally or not at all, and keeps a record that never fades. Your Gemini Sun stands between, a messenger sending signals across the gap: questions, jokes, theories, a long careful letter. People think you are easy-going. A few know you are keeping the midnight hour.","Scorpio Moon and Taurus Rising face each other across the wheel, both fixed, so need and manner balance on a long beam: calm and comfort on the outside, intensity and truth on the inside, and neither will give way. The Gemini Sun sits at an awkward remove from the Moon and a sign from the Rising, so it is the go-between, curious about the whole arrangement and a little baffled by it. The Moon is in its fall, learning strength through humility.","Calm that has depth. You can sit with an enormous feeling and not flinch, ask the question that opens the hidden thing, and keep a confidence for life. In a crisis you are slow to panic, quick to understand and unusually loyal, and you speak with the voice of someone who has thought it through.","The Rising keeps the surface warm and the Moon keeps the account, so a hurt can be filed politely and held for years. The Sun explains it away cleverly and the matter stays put. Growth is saying “that cost me something” in the first week, in the plain, kind voice you already have."],"gemini-sagittarius-aries":["Three travellers meet at a crossroads. The Gemini Sun reads every signpost aloud, with variations. The Sagittarius Moon has already chosen a direction, on faith, and is whistling. The Aries Rising has run ahead to check that the road is any good and will be back with a report, a blister and an opinion. Nobody in this party is afraid of the open road. The only quarrel is over whether to stop and read the map or simply go.","Gemini Sun and Sagittarius Moon face each other across the wheel, both mutable, so what you are and what you need are two halves of one curiosity: the particular and the whole, the question and the belief. The Aries Rising is a trine to the Moon and a sextile to the Sun, so the manner supports both with energy and courage. Two fire lights keep the chart warm and the air Sun keeps it talking. It is a lively arrangement with very little caution in it.","Contagious optimism. You make learning feel like an adventure, you encourage people to try the thing they were afraid of, and you tell the story of the trip so well that others want to go. You are brave, funny, generous with ideas and hard to discourage.","With the Sun curious, the Moon hopeful and the Rising ready, there is no brake. Plans are made faster than they can be kept, and honesty arrives as bluntness. Growth is writing down the cost of the next promise before making it, and finishing one trip before booking the next."],"gemini-sagittarius-taurus":["You are standing between two open doors, one to the orchard and one to the road, holding a map whose edges nobody has labelled. The Taurus Rising is the orchard: calm, solid, unhurried, with a lovely voice and a September sweetness that makes people stay. The Sagittarius Moon is the road, needing space, adventure and faith in tomorrow. Your Gemini Sun, directly opposite the Moon, wants to know about both and be on first-name terms with each. You are an easy host with a packed bag in the hall.","Gemini Sun and Sagittarius Moon face each other across the wheel, both mutable, so what you are and what you need are two halves of one curiosity: the detail and the horizon. The Taurus Rising stands a sign from the Sun and at an awkward remove from the Moon, so the stay-put manner you wear sits uneasily over a need to roam. That is why you may seem more settled than you feel. The Sun carries the argument by talking about both.","Rooted curiosity. You bring home stories, recipes, words and strangers and you make them part of the household. You are sociable, optimistic, calm in a crisis and good at making an unfamiliar place feel inviting. People trust you with both their secrets and their travel plans.","The Rising promises to stay and the Moon plans to leave, and the Sun keeps both versions of the story going. Others may feel misled when the packed bag finally leaves the hall. Growth is telling the people you love, early, which door you are looking at today."],"gemini-capricorn-aries":["By fifty you will understand that the reserve you took for coldness was a good instinct about timing, and the speed you were embarrassed by was courage that had not yet learned its season. The Aries Rising goes first. The Capricorn Moon, a square away, feels privately and manages feeling like a task, so the dash is followed by a long, serious pause. Your Gemini Sun talks its way between the two, making jokes where a plan would be better. People see a quick, funny starter. Later they see someone who always finishes.","The Capricorn Moon squares the Aries Rising, both cardinal, so the need for structure and the habit of leaping meet at a right angle and neither backs down. The Gemini Sun sits at an awkward remove from the Moon and makes a friendly sextile with the Rising, so curiosity sides with the leap and the Moon is left to supply the discipline. The Moon sits in detriment here, working against the grain, so tenderness has to be learned. Each light is a different kind of fast.","Ambition with a sense of humour. You can plan seriously and act boldly, and you make hard work sound like a good story. You are capable of long preparation for a quick, perfectly timed move, and others trust you to lead because you are both brave and prepared.","The Moon does the worrying silently and the Rising does the leaping loudly, so people see confidence and miss the strain. The Sun supplies a joke to cover the gap. Growth is saying “this is heavy” to someone who can help carry it, and letting the answer be slow."],"gemini-capricorn-taurus":["You are the friendliest voice at the table and the one who tells the least about yourself, and both are completely sincere. The Gemini Sun trades stories, jokes and questions all evening. The Capricorn Moon feels privately and manages feeling like a task, so it is the one in the back with the accounts. The Taurus Rising, in easy trine with it, gives you the lovely voice and the unhurried calm that make this arrangement look effortless. You are a loom with a telegraph line attached: steady work, and quick news.","Two earth lights and an air Sun. Capricorn Moon and Taurus Rising are a trine, so need and manner cooperate with ease: reserved, reliable, built to last. The Gemini Sun is the outsider, at an awkward remove from the Moon and a sign from the Rising, curious and chatty in a household that prefers to be useful. The Moon sits in detriment here, working against the grain, so tenderness has to be learned. The Sun supplies the conversation, the others supply the foundation.","Reliable wit. You can make a serious subject sound easy, you meet deadlines with a smile and you keep your promises without announcing them. You are a calm presence in a messy room, and the kind of colleague, friend or parent who makes a plan and makes people laugh while it is carried out.","Feeling is managed like a task and discussed like a topic, so what is happening in you can be described precisely and still go unfelt. The Rising makes it all look composed. Growth is letting one feeling stay unorganised for an evening, and telling one person, without a joke, that it is there."],"gemini-aquarius-aries":["After the meeting has ended, you are still at the whiteboard, drawing lines between people who have never met and saying “those two should talk”. The Aries Rising makes the first call, usually before the plan is finished. The Aquarius Moon, friendly and cool, needs freedom, friendship and room to be strange. Your Gemini Sun, in trine with it, is the messenger who carries the idea from one corner of the network to another. People find you quick, generous and a little hard to pin to one group.","Two air lights and a fire Rising make an arc of ease: Gemini Sun and Aquarius Moon are a trine, and the Aries Rising makes a friendly sextile with each, so the three lights cooperate and almost nothing is in conflict. Ideas flow, the manner pushes them into action, and the Moon asks only that nobody try to own the result. The ease is the risk: with no friction, the chart can stay brilliant and unfinished, a very good network that never builds a house.","Inventive connection. You introduce people, ideas and fields that should have met earlier, you act on a good thought before it cools, and you leave others feeling that the future is slightly more possible. You are generous with credit and unbothered by convention.","Everything flows, so nothing is forced to land. The Moon prefers detachment, the Rising prefers motion and the Sun enjoys the discussion, so plans stay as constellations. Growth is picking one line on the whiteboard and doing the dull work of making it a bridge."],"gemini-aquarius-taurus":["People take the calm, friendly manner for conventionality, and are startled by the first idea you share. The Taurus Rising gives you a lovely voice, an unhurried air and the look of someone who owns a good coat and a regular parking space. The Aquarius Moon, a square away, needs friends, freedom and room to be strange. Your Gemini Sun, in easy trine with the Moon, is the one who has read about the satellite pass and will tell you, at length, when to look up. The surface is traditional. The household is not.","Two air lights and an earth Rising. Gemini Sun and Aquarius Moon are a trine, so curiosity and the need for freedom run together as easily as two friends on a long walk. The Taurus Rising squares the Moon, both fixed, so the settled, sensual manner argues stubbornly with the need to be odd and unattached. It stands a sign from the Sun. The result is an experimental mind in a conservative coat, and a good deal of friction about when to take it off.","Friendly originality. You make the unusual sound welcoming, you introduce new ideas without alarming anyone and you have the patience to see them through. People trust you with change because you look as if you would never rush it, and you hold the door for those who do.","The Rising resists change and the Moon demands it, so you can argue for freedom in the evening and keep the same routine in the morning. The Sun enjoys the discussion. Growth is changing one fixed habit this week and telling a friend, who will not let you quietly revert."],"gemini-pisces-aries":["You can talk for an hour and feel that nothing was said, and sit silent for a minute and feel that everything was. The Gemini Sun is a mind that thinks by speaking, and the Aries Rising speaks first and fastest. The Pisces Moon, a neighbour to the Rising and square to the Sun, feels what belongs to other people as well as what belongs to you, and needs music, water and solitude to sort it. People get the chatter. You get the hymn heard through the wall.","Gemini Sun and Pisces Moon square each other, both mutable, so mind and feeling keep crossing: the Sun wants to name things, the Moon wants to dissolve them. The Aries Rising sits one sign from the Moon, which means the quick, direct front door is bolted onto a very porous room. Three different elements and no shared ground make for variety and a certain loneliness. The Rising acts, the Moon absorbs, and the Sun tries to keep up with the commentary.","Imaginative quickness. You catch a mood and make it into a story, a song or a joke before others have noticed it, and you can enter a stranger’s feeling without losing your own footing for long. Your gifts show most in words, music and the small act of timing a kindness perfectly.","Absorbing everyone’s weather and then outrunning your own, you may leave a room tired in a way that nothing explains. Talk is used to dilute the feeling. Growth is a regular silence with water or music in it, and one friend to whom you say the true thing without the joke."],"gemini-pisces-taurus":["You carry it in the hands and the breath: hands that fold, shape and fidget as if working something that cannot be said, and a breath held a little high in the chest. The Pisces Moon feels everything, including what belongs to others, and needs solitude, music and water to find its edges. The Taurus Rising, a friendly sextile away, gives the whole matter a calm, solid, lovely-voiced front, so nobody guesses. Your Gemini Sun squares the Moon and talks, folding feelings into paper boats and setting them on the current.","Gemini Sun and Pisces Moon square each other, both mutable, so thought and feeling keep crossing: the Sun wants to name, the Moon wants to dissolve. The Taurus Rising is a friendly sextile to the Moon and a neighbour to the Sun, so the manner supports the water, giving it a shore, a voice and a routine. The effect is a porous interior inside a very well-behaved exterior. Venus smooths the surface, Neptune loosens what lies under it, and Mercury attempts to keep notes.","Gentle fluency. You can talk someone through a sorrow without making them feel managed, find the right word at the right time and make something beautiful out of a passing mood. People feel safe near the calm and understood by the words, and often come back for both.","Absorbing the room’s feelings behind a calm face, you may be exhausted without a visible cause. The Sun explains it as tiredness, a busy week, anything but weather. Growth is asking, quietly and often, which of these feelings are yours, and giving the water an hour alone each day."]});
